The clause's trigger is that the manager has approved the correction in writing. Only the "person gave an explicit yes" candidate matches that situation: a written approval is an explicit yes, and the manager is the person whose approval is needed.

The other candidates (shipment lateness, session state, invoice editing, helper agents, supplier language table, carrier answers) are not mentioned in the clause. The "has not answered" candidate is the opposite of the trigger.

